      "headline": "Glide Identity, ex Coinbase",
      "about": "I used to work at Coinbase doing application security.\n\nAlso a owner of - \nhttps://leguprecovery.com and https://leguprx.com\n\nI worked at Stratum Security as an application security consultant. Here I worked on application penetration tests and code review.\n\nI worked at Floor and Decor as the application security manager / lead helping to build the SSDLC processes, pentesting, and the application security program as a whole. Here I was responsible for the creation and operation of the application security program.\n\nI worked at Kimberly-Clark as an application security consultant / SME / everything in between type role where I helped to build the application security program and pentest apps - basically I was a contact for developers to figure out security related tasks while helping to run the program initiatives while also performing pentesting.\n\nLots of work with figuring out how to best work with CI/CD pipelines / processes ensuring developers can still release code while maintaining security requirements -\n\nAlso worked at General Motors in the appsec space (after my undergrad). \n\nSoftware dev - Python, Java, C/C++,. NET, C#, PHP, no-code apps etc. Fortify, Checkmarx, Web Inspect, AppScan etc. - I’ve used a decent amount of tools in my career. Burp Suite Professional, WAFs, penetration testing (web / mobile speciality), secure code reviews / software architecture - application security speciality, bug bounties (been on top 10 leaderboard multiple times), etc. \n\nCertified GIAC GWAPT\n\nOpinions here are my own.",
